"""assimregion_connectome_similarity_pairs.csv | Supplementary Fig. S11 (04_figures/supp_assimregion/figS_assimregion_A4.py)

Recovered statistical-analysis script | reproducibility package | Fig. 3 track.

WHAT THIS SCRIPT COMPUTES
    This code computes similarity between functional connectivity (FC)
    matrices derived from different MRI runs of a monetary incentive delay
    (MID) task, comparing an "assimilated region" version of the data
    against repeated task runs. For each of two conditions (feedback-hit
    and anticipation-hit), it averages FC matrices across win-magnitude
    subconditions, extracts the upper-triangular connectivity values for
    five repeat runs and one reference "act" run, then computes Pearson
    correlations across finite entries: pairwise correlations among the
    five repeats ("repeat" pair_type) and correlations of each repeat
    against the reference run ("region" pair_type). One row of the output
    table represents a single such pairwise comparison, identified by
    condition, pair_type, and the specific pair label, with the
    correlation coefficient recorded as r.

INPUT FILES
    task_fc_raw_217x217_7runs.mat

OUTPUT FILE
    assimregion_connectome_similarity_pairs.csv
    written to OUT_DIR (default /tmp/recovery_scratch/fig3)
    reference copy in this package: 04_figures/supp_assimregion/data/assimregion_connectome_similarity_pairs.csv

STATISTICAL TESTS
    descriptive summary only (no inferential test in the recovered cell)

RUNNABLE ON A LAPTOP
    conditional on the input files above being present on this machine

SEED
    not applicable (deterministic computation)

